@dagnam/vis bundles three fonts so that PNGs are drawn the same on every
machine. They ship in dist/node/fonts/ with their licence texts.

Inter 4.1
  Copyright (c) 2016 The Inter Project Authors (https://github.com/rsms/inter)
  Licence: SIL Open Font License 1.1, dist/node/fonts/OFL.txt
  Files: Inter-Regular.ttf, Inter-Bold.ttf

Unbounded (static instances, wght 400, 500 and 700, Latin subset)
  Copyright 2022 The Unbounded Project Authors (https://github.com/googlefonts/unbounded)
  Licence: SIL Open Font License 1.1, dist/node/fonts/OFL-Unbounded.txt
  Files: Unbounded-Regular.ttf, Unbounded-Medium.ttf, Unbounded-Bold.ttf

Moonhouse
  Copyright (c) 2013 by NimaVisual. All rights reserved.
  Licence: the font's own embedded licence, dist/node/fonts/moonhouse/LICENSE-NOTE.txt
  File: moonhouse/moonhouse.ttf, byte for byte as received
  Its terms require written permission from NimaVisual for redistribution. It
  is bundled on the package owner's confirmation (recorded 2026-10-25) that
  Dagnam has that permission; the grant itself is not kept in this repository.
  Removing it is one directory (src/node/fonts/moonhouse) and one
  entry in FONT_FILES (src/node/render-png.ts); the wordmark of the brand card and
  the display text of the social card then fall back to another face.

Third-party code. gifenc is installed as a dependency (not bundled into dist/;
npm installs it with its own licence file). mp4-muxer and webm-muxer are
bundled: their published ESM builds are copied unmodified into
dist/export/vendor/ by scripts/vendor-muxers.mjs, and the licence text for both
is below.

